(Bug #27 regression: stacked periods close nested clauses one level each
 (LANGUAGE.md, Closing more than one level). Repeat nested inside For
 each: the first period closes the Repeat (the innermost clause), the
 second closes the For each, so "after" runs once. Before the fix the
 Repeat never consumed its period, so the second period had nothing to
 close and the program failed with `Expected a statement, got Period`.
 Expected: r, r, r, r, after.)

For each n from 1 to 2,
    Repeat 2 times, Print "r"..
Print "after".